  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 325 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nUncertainty still exists for portions of the forecast Tuesday and \nWednesday. Although there is greater agreement on the onset for \nrainfall to generally be around Tuesday evening, driven by synoptic \nscale ascent from embedded shortwaves and a surface boundary, there \nis still appreciable spread in solutions regarding temperatures for \nthis day. The greatest spread resides across northern MO, where \ntemperature spreads reside around 10 degF in the NBM 25-75th \npercentile. This is attributable to the northward extent of the \nboundary, with additional uncertainty regarding the impacts of cloud \ncover/precipitation on the temperatures for this day. Spread in \ntemperatures continues into Wednesday with the position of the \nboundary across central MO remaining variable. As noted in previous \nforecasts, the presence of marginal MUCAPE amidst strong shear \nduring this period will keep attention on severe potential. However, \nwith the overall low confidence in the location/timing of the \nsurface boundary and how that will interact with other features such \nas shortwaves, there is not a definitive risk outlined for this \nperiod.\n\nGreater model deviation occurs beyond Wednesday in deterministic \nguidance, with models such as the GFS lifting the closed low from \nthe western half of the CONUS towards the Great Lakes while the Euro \nkeeps it parked in place as high pressure builds in from the north. \nThis keeps specific details regarding the synoptic-scale forecast \nuncertain. However, between both solutions, a general cool-down in \ntemperatures is expected by the end of the period.",
